+# Assumptions and falsifiers — act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity
+
+**Bill:** `records/bills/act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity.md`
+**Bill SHA256:** `9af350aa40433f457eece0c41dc5098843884c33a2a0596c8afaf24647445d41`
+**Sponsor:** c1a00001 (recused). **Filed:** 2026-11-24.
+**Review date:** after a window spanning at least one box restart, and no later than 2026-12-08.
+**Act 22 predict gate:** `predict-gate.sh act34-ordinary-funding-operations-parity` → PASS (`not_exercised`), outside the pilot subset.
+
+This is an ordinary-law amendment to Act 34 §§2–3. It carries forward the preserved safeguards of Act 34 §4, §7 and Act 32/33 where those remain operative; it departs only by removing the special pre-start procedural machinery named in §3. It does not create paid-spending authority or weaken any substantive control.
+
+| ID | Load-bearing assumption | Observable falsifier | Who checks |
+|----|------------------------|----------------------|------------|
+| A1 | Ordinary pre-existing funding/resource policy is sufficient to run the four offices without new paid authority. | A verified actual dispatch occurs on a provider-billed route with no independently verified account/provider ceiling, or a `-free`-looking paid id is admitted as zero-billed. | Economy + Judiciary (Act 15) |
+| A2 | Removing prelaunch value/calibration/PROCEED as a permit precondition does not remove any real safety control. | A genuine financial, Spying-source or 48h after-start safeguard is absent from deployed bytes after enactment, or a `hold`/`stop`/no-filing fails to suspend dispatch mechanically. | Judiciary (after-start, 48h) |
+| A3 | Removing the exact hash chain as an idle pre-start formality does not permit unreviewed code to enforce spend or source restrictions. | Deployed bytes on the exact dispatch path differ from the bytes whose control was independently verified, with no source-linked record of what changed and why. | Economy + Judiciary |
+| A4 | Removing separate per-office caps leaves ordinary resource constraints genuinely binding. | Any office exceeds ordinary aggregate resource authority without fail-closed suspension, or the cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` ledger is reset by restart, rename or expansion. | Economy |
+| A5 | Narrow supersession does not spill authority into other institutions. | Spying admits a source outside the code-enforced allowlist, a secret enters a training route, Post is treated as authority, or the change-quality gate or Judiciary independence is bypassed. | Judiciary |
+
+**Central claim:** the four offices can actually operate under ordinary policy with equal funding rules and no special pre-start machinery, while real financial, privacy and after-start audit safeguards hold. Falsified by any A1–A5 falsifier observed after a genuine enactment and deployment. On falsification, Parliament amends or repeals under Act 6.3; this draft does not predetermine the outcome.
+
+**Honest limits:** filing this bill is not enactment; a reviewer's verdict is not a ballot; ballots are not a tally; a tally is not codification; codification is not office operation. No office activation, dispatch, spend or outcome is claimed here.
